# Commit Before EAS Build/Submit

Before running any `eas build` or `eas submit` command:

1. Stage all relevant changed files with `git add`
2. Create a commit with a clear, descriptive message summarizing what changed and why
3. Verify the commit succeeded before proceeding to the EAS command

```bash
# ❌ BAD — pushing to EAS without committing
eas build --platform ios --profile production

# ✅ GOOD — commit first, then build
git add -A
git commit -m "Add debug notifications to LogTransactionIntent for automation troubleshooting"
eas build --platform ios --profile production
```

Never skip the commit step, even for small or temporary changes.
